            "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
            "bytes": 125422,
            "dimensions": {
              "originalWidth": 1680,
              "originalHeight": 945
            }
          },
          "body_html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.7rem\">As of 2026, <strong>Optical Circuit Switching</strong> has evolved from a specialized research technology into a cornerstone of <strong>hyperscale data center infrastructure</strong>.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 1.7rem\">This shift was heavily driven by <strong>Google's</strong> successful large-scale deployment of its <strong>Jupiter network fabric</strong> and <strong>TPU supercomputer clusters</strong>.</span></p><p></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "type": "image",
          "variant": "text_aside",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "COLOR",
            "background_color": "#f1f1f1",
            "image_position": "right",
            "image_size": "small",
            "image_opacity": 0.5,
            "image_opacity_color": "#000000",
            "zoom_on_click": true,
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 3,
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO"
          },
          "image_role": "content",
          "media": {
            "path": "resources/images/6.jpg",
            "alt": "6.jpg",
            "source_asset": "6.jpg",
            "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
            "bytes": 154436,
            "dimensions": {
              "width": 945,
              "height": 945,
              "originalWidth": 1680,
              "originalHeight": 945
            }
          },
          "body_html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.7rem\">By eliminating <strong>power-intensive</strong> Optical-Electrical-Optical conversions, OCS has enabled substantial reductions in <strong>power consumption</strong> and <strong>capital expenditure</strong>.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 1.7rem\">At the same time, it delivers the <strong>ultra-low latency</strong> and <strong>jitter-free performance</strong> required by modern <strong>artificial intelligence</strong> workloads.</span></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "type": "text",
          "variant": "paragraph",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "COLOR",
            "background_color": "#f1f1f1",
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 3,
            "padding_bottom": 3,
            "marker_color_contrast": "AUTO"
          },
          "body_html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.7rem\">While <strong>hyperscalers</strong> currently lead in production-scale deployments, the broader industry ecosystem is rapidly expanding. <strong>System integrators</strong>, <strong>technology suppliers</strong>, and <strong>network operators</strong> are actively developing new <strong>optically enabled architectures</strong>. To accelerate this transition, open standards bodies like the <strong>Open Compute Project</strong> are working to ensure <strong>interoperability</strong> and lower the barrier to entry for all operators.</span></p><p>The optical networking ecosystem relies on collaboration across <strong>several distinct layers of the industry</strong>.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "type": "image",
          "variant": "full",
          "style": {
            "background_type": "LIGHT",
            "card_mode": "WHITE",
            "image_opacity": 0.5,
            "image_opacity_color": "#000000",
            "zoom_on_click": false,
            "attached_to_next": false,
            "padding_top": 0,
            "padding_bottom": 0,
